# The two-variable fragment of the example IMDB MLN in Figure 1 of:
#
#   Mihalkova, Huynh, and Mooney, "Mapping and Revising Markov Logic
#   Networks for Transfer Learning", AAAI 2007.
#
# These are the first three published clauses with their published weights.
# The paper's fourth clause is omitted because it uses three variables.
# WorkedFor is renamed to the benchmark's usual WorkedUnder spelling, and
# independent rule variables are alpha-renamed to the two symbols X and Y.
# The paper uses typed person/movie domains; this file flattens them into the
# single finite domain supported by the current WFOMC problem representation.

1.5 Director(X) | Actor(X)
0.1 MovieMember(Y,X) | ~Director(X)
1.3 ~WorkedUnder(X,Y) | ~Director(X)

entity = 4
